  "description": "The authentication virtual server **auth_vs1**, now renamed to **auth_vs1_new**, is active on IP\u202f192.168.1.10 (IPv4\u2011IPv6 address\u202f10.0.0.5) listening on port\u202f443. It is a **CONTENT**\u2011type, SSL\u2011servicetype vserver with AppFlow logging **ENABLED**, authentication turned **ON**, and the authentication domain set to **example.com**. The server\u2019s current state is **UP** and its overall status flag is **1**. It is enabled (**state\u202fENABLED**) and has a comment of \u201cPrimary authentication vserver\u201d. Client timeout is 300\u202fseconds, failed\u2011login timeout is 30\u202fseconds, and the maximum number of login attempts is 3. The client\u2010side access attribute (curaaausers) shows 12 users, and group extraction is **true**. The vserver is bound to the certificate key **cert1**, but the value field reports \u201cCertkey not bound\u201d. Load\u2011balancing weight is 50 and the weight\u2011type identifier (**vstype**) is 2.\n\nFor fail\u2011over and caching, the primary backup vserver is **backup_vs1**, while the associated cache vserver is **cache_vs1** with a **TRANSPARENT** cache type. Traffic is bound at the **REQUEST** bind point, and the bind profile uses **httpProfile1** for HTTP and **tcpProfile1** for TCP. Redirection is configured to **CACHE** with the redirect URL **https://cache.example.com**. The vserver is linked to policy **policy1** (listen priority\u202f5) and policy binding **policyBind1**, with precedence set to **RULE**, priority\u202f10, and a range of 255. Sessions persist using **ENABLED** SO persistence, a persistence timeout of 120\u202fseconds, and a threshold of 80. The secondary flag is **false**, disable\u2011primary\u2011on\u2011down is **ENABLED**, and down\u2011state flush is **DISABLED**. The service name is **svc1**, the TCP profile is **tcpProfile1**, the SO method is **HEALTH**, and the traffic management daemon identifier (**td**) is 0. Finally, the new\u2011name field reflects the updated name **auth_vs1_new**, and the NG name is **ng1**.",
